    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 starting lineup for July 22 is headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who carries an impressive 74.56 score into his matchup against Hughes. His outlook is bolstered significantly by a 14% park factor boost and a favorable platoon advantage, making him our highest-ceiling play. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** (70.97) stands out as an elite play against the vulnerable Kelly; his ability to leverage his leadoff spot against a weak opposing starter provides the best efficiency-to-risk ratio on the board today. **Drake Baldwin** (67.31) also merits mention as a strong start, as his xwOBA of .387 and favorable leadoff position against King elevate him well above the standard catcher projection.\n\nStrategic decisions on the periphery were dictated by our extreme weight on stolen base potential and platoon splits. **Coby Mayo** (60.25) earned the start at 3B primarily because his matchup against Bennett allows for a \"slow delivery\" exploit that juices his steal probability. Conversely, **Gunnar Henderson** (58.50) and **Heliot Ramos** (58.17) see their scores tempered; **Henderson** faces a significant platoon penalty against Rivera, while **Ramos** contends with a wind-in factor that suppresses his power profile against Lugo. The most difficult personnel decision was leaving **Nasim Nunez** (55.36) on the bench. Despite his switch-hitting versatility and favorable park factors at his venue, his ninth-place spot in the batting order created a drag on his efficiency, ultimately keeping him out of the starting nine in favor of higher-leverage lineup spots. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of the mid-summer schedule. While **Kyle Tucker** (66.04) continues to be an automatic start, we are monitoring the matchup against Nola, whose ability to suppress runners poses a minor threat to our overall stolen base pursuit. We have avoided deploying **Miguel Vargas** (47.01) and **Jorge Polanco** (41.20) as their projected efficiencies against Alexander and Henderson respectively fall too close to our \"Below Floor\" threshold. Managers should keep a close eye on any late-inning weather alerts, but as it stands, the combination of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Drake Baldwin** forms the core of an Austin Waves squad well-positioned to capitalize on today\u2019s favorable SP matchups.",
